 *OOP Concept Demonstrated* 

The program uses runtime polymorphism through the abstract ""PaymentMethod"" class. The ""processPayment()"" function is overridden by each derived payment class, allowing different payment methods to process transactions according to their own implementation.

 *Objective* 

To understand how abstract classes, inheritance, runtime polymorphism, and smart pointers can be used to design a flexible payment gateway supporting multiple payment methods.

 *Key Concepts Demonstrated* 
* 
- Abstraction – Defines a common payment interface using the abstract "PaymentMethod" class.
- Inheritance – Payment classes inherit common transaction details from "PaymentMethod".
- Polymorphism – Each payment type implements "processPayment()" differently.
- Pure Virtual Function – Defines the required payment processing interface.
- Function Overriding – Derived classes provide their own implementation of "processPayment()".
- Encapsulation – Payment-specific information is kept inside the respective classes.
- Smart Pointers – "unique_ptr" manages payment objects automatically.
- Vector – Stores multiple payment objects in a single collection.
- Runtime Polymorphism – The correct payment processing function is selected at runtime.
